## Tech stack

- Java 21 + Spring Boot 3.5 (via `org.springframework.boot:spring-boot-starter-parent`)
- Maven build with quality gates in `verify`: Jacoco check (≥ 85 % line / ≥ 75 % branch per class), PIT (≥ 75 %), Surefire + Failsafe
- Jenkins CI (declarative pipeline)
- Helm chart for Kubernetes deployment
- Prometheus metrics on `{{contextPath}}/actuator/prometheus`

## Local build

```sh
./mvnw -q -DskipTests package   # build
./mvnw -q verify                 # tests + quality gates (as CI)
./mvnw spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=local   # run locally on port {{appPort}}
```

The app exposes:

- `GET {{contextPath}}/actuator/health/liveness`
- `GET {{contextPath}}/actuator/health/readiness`
- `GET {{contextPath}}/actuator/prometheus`

## Configuration

| Variable | Required | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `JWT_ISSUER_URI` | yes, when the service authenticates callers | OAuth2 issuer URL of the identity provider (Helm: `jwt.issuerUri`); the `local` profile sets a local default |
| `JWT_AUDIENCE` | no, defaults to `{{artifactId}}` | audience a token must carry (Helm: `jwt.audience`) |
| `DB_URL` | yes, when the service has a SQL database | JDBC URL, e.g. `jdbc:postgresql://<host>:5432/<db>` (Helm: `database.url`); the `local` profile points at the docker-compose Postgres |
| `DB_USER` | yes, when the service has a SQL database | database user (Helm: `database.username`) |
| `DB_PASSWORD` | yes, when the service has a SQL database | database password, no default; from the credentials Secret (Helm: `credentials.existingSecret`, key `DB_PASSWORD`) |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | no, defaults to `INFO` | application log level |

Remove the two `JWT_*` rows for a service without authentication and the three `DB_*` rows for one without a database.

